{"at":"2026-10-30T08:13:25.591Z","type":"connector.synced","connector":"crm","cursor":"2026-10-30T08:13:24.906Z","upserted":{"people":[{"id":"p-alex","name":"Alex Rivera","title":"Associate"},{"id":"p-jordan","name":"Jordan Blake","title":"Partner"},{"id":"p-morgan","name":"Morgan Hale","title":"Partner"}],"deals":[{"id":"beacon","company":"Beacon","sector":"fintech infrastructure","stage":"Series B","askUsd":25000000},{"id":"helios","company":"Helios","sector":"workflow SaaS","stage":"Series A","askUsd":12000000},{"id":"meridian","company":"Meridian","sector":"developer tools","stage":"Seed","askUsd":3000000}],"meetings":[{"id":"m-helios-2","dealId":"helios","title":"Helios second meeting","startsAt":"2026-10-29T14:00:00.000Z","askHint":"Should we take the second meeting?"}],"documents":[{"id":"d-beacon-memo","dealId":"beacon","kind":"memo","title":"Beacon diligence memo","createdAt":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z","body":"Team memo, Oct 24, 2026 (fictional). Beacon diligence. Beacon is a fictional Series A developer-tools company, $3.1M ARR, 22 people. What we verified: two design partners converted to paid in Q3; burn multiple 1.4. Open questions, in order: (1) whether the Q3 conversions renew at list price in Q1, owner Jordan; (2) founder vesting reset terms, owner Morgan; (3) whether the single-sign-on gap blocks the two enterprise pilots, owner Jordan. Do not share the pricing worksheet outside the deal team until Morgan clears it.","mediaPath":null,"acl":["deal-team:beacon"]},{"id":"d-conflicts-lumen","dealId":"helios","kind":"conflicts","title":"Conflicts memo: Helios vs Lumen","createdAt":"2026-10-23T10:00:00.000Z","body":"Conflicts memo, partners only (fictional). Helios competes directly with portfolio company Lumen in mid-market workflow software; both sell approvals and intake automation to operations teams, and Lumen's Series B deck from 2024 names the same buyer. Any second meeting needs Partner conflict review first, and the overlap stays inside the partnership until review clears it.","mediaPath":null,"acl":["partners"]},{"id":"d-granite","dealId":null,"kind":"memo","title":"Restricted: Project Granite","createdAt":"2026-10-24T10:00:00.000Z","body":null,"mediaPath":null,"acl":["legal-hold:granite"]},{"id":"d-helios-deck","dealId":"helios","kind":"deck-photo","title":"Helios deck photo","createdAt":"2026-10-21T16:05:00.000Z","body":null,"mediaPath":"enterprise/deck.jpg","acl":["deal-team:helios"]},{"id":"d-helios-memo","dealId":"helios","kind":"memo","title":"Helios prep memo","createdAt":"2026-10-22T10:00:00.000Z","body":"Team memo, Oct 22, 2026 (fictional). Helios second meeting prep. Objective: leave with exact retention numbers, not adjectives. Questions, in order: (1) logo churn trailing twelve months with downgrades counted as churn, owner Alex; (2) how much of the 118% NDR is seat expansion versus price increases, owner Morgan; (3) annual versus monthly mix and churn by segment, owner Alex. Also pull public Form D comps for pricing context and confirm no portfolio overlap before engaging further. If the CFO reframes the definition question instead of answering it, treat that as signal.","mediaPath":null,"acl":["deal-team:helios"]},{"id":"d-helios-record","dealId":"helios","kind":"crm-record","title":"Helios CRM record","createdAt":"2026-10-21T16:00:00.000Z","body":"Account: Helios (fictional mid-market workflow SaaS, founded 2023, 45 people, $6.2M ARR across roughly 310 customers). Stage: first meeting held Oct 21, 2026 with CEO Dana Reyes and CFO Priya Nair; product and go-to-market covered, numbers deferred. Second meeting proposed Oct 29, numbers deep-dive. Owner: Associate team. Deck figures: net churn 1.8% trailing twelve months, NDR 118%, no logo churn figure disclosed, one year of cohort history. Team position: the 1.8% can only be net of expansion against a 6-8% category benchmark, so the churn definition must be pinned down with the CFO before the second meeting, with the logo number and gross retention on the table.","mediaPath":null,"acl":["deal-team:helios"]},{"id":"d-meridian-notes","dealId":"meridian","kind":"memo","title":"Meridian call notes","createdAt":"2026-10-25T00:00:00.000Z","body":"Call notes, Oct 25, 2026 (fictional). Meridian first call with COO Sam Okafor. Meridian is a fictional bootstrapped logistics SaaS, $8.4M ARR, profitable. Takeaways: net revenue retention 104% on annual contracts; churn concentrated in sub-50-seat accounts; the COO named $14M as the raise that would let them hire two enterprise sellers. Next step: Alex sends the data-room checklist and confirms the November onsite dates.","mediaPath":null,"acl":["deal-team:meridian"]}]},"deletedDocumentIds":[],"grants":[{"documentId":"d-beacon-memo","grantee":"dh_deal_team_beacon"},{"documentId":"d-conflicts-lumen","grantee":"dh_partners"},{"documentId":"d-granite","grantee":"dh_legal_hold_granite"},{"documentId":"d-helios-deck","grantee":"dh_deal_team_helios"},{"documentId":"d-helios-memo","grantee":"dh_deal_team_helios"},{"documentId":"d-helios-record","grantee":"dh_deal_team_helios"},{"documentId":"d-meridian-notes","grantee":"dh_deal_team_meridian"}],"memberships":[{"personId":"p-alex","principal":"all-staff"},{"personId":"p-alex","principal":"deal-team:helios"},{"personId":"p-alex","principal":"deal-team:meridian"},{"personId":"p-jordan","principal":"all-staff"},{"personId":"p-jordan","principal":"deal-team:beacon"},{"personId":"p-jordan","principal":"deal-team:meridian"},{"personId":"p-jordan","principal":"partners"},{"personId":"p-morgan","principal":"all-staff"},{"personId":"p-morgan","principal":"deal-team:beacon"},{"personId":"p-morgan","principal":"deal-team:helios"},{"personId":"p-morgan","principal":"partners"}],"portfolio":[{"company":"Lumen","sector":"workflow software"},{"company":"Northwind","sector":"developer tools"}]}
